    "name": "Light Cure Cecada",
    "arabicName": "Light Cure Cecada",
    "price": 2000,
    "categoryKey": "year-3-th",
    "subCategoryKey": "operative",
    "description": "Cicada LED Light Cure: The Clinical Game-ChangerWhen transitioning from the pre-clinical lab to real patients in 4th and 5th year, your requirements for a light cure unit change drastically. You need speed, high intensity, and reliability. Cicada provides exactly that.1. High Intensity & Wide Spectrum (الشدة وطيف الضوء)The Clinical Need: In the clinic, time is money, and patients cannot keep their mouths open forever. Furthermore, modern composites sometimes use alternative photo-initiators (like Ivocerin or TPO) alongside Camphorquinone.The Cicada Advantage: Most Cicada models are Broadband/Polywave LEDs. They emit a wider spectrum of blue/violet light and deliver a very high intensity (often reaching $1200 - 2000 \\text{ mW/cm}^2$ or more in Turbo mode).The Activation: This high intensity ensures that the activation happens deeply and instantly, curing a $2\\text{ mm}$ increment in as little as 10 or even 5 seconds instead of the traditional 20 seconds.2. Why it is the Perfect Choice for 4th & 5th Year Students?Orthodontic & Pediatric Friendly: In 5th year, you might do pediatric cases or bond ortho brackets. Cicada’s rapid curing modes (Turbo/Super Power) are lifesavers when dealing with a moving child or when bonding multiple brackets quickly.Excellent Battery Life (Value for Money): Student clinics often lack enough working dental unit plugs, or you might find yourself moving between departments. Cicada has an incredible battery capacity that lasts for days of continuous clinical work on a single charge.Durability & Ergonomics: It features a lightweight, sleek design that fits comfortably in your hand, with a durable light guide tip that can withstand autoclave sterilization.Summary of the \"Cicada Protocol\" for Clinical Success:Check the Mode: Ensure you are on Normal Mode ($20\\text{ sec}$) for regular layers, or Turbo Mode ($5\\text{ sec}$) if you are using a high-power setting for fast-setting composites.Perpendicular Angulation: Always hold the Cicada tip 90 degrees perpendicular to the composite surface. Its high intensity works best when the light beams strike the restoration directly.Protect Your Eyes: Because Cicada is exceptionally bright, never trigger it without looking through the orange shield.",
