    "price": 200,
    "categoryKey": "clinical",
    "subCategoryKey": "remove-",
    "description": "Premium Alginate Impression Material – Normal Set\nThe Reliable Choice for Accurate Primary Impressions & Study Models\nThe Smooth Start to Your Crown & Bridge Workflows\n\nBefore beginning your crown preparation, capturing an accurate baseline is essential. This high-quality Alginate Impression Material is specifically selected for taking precise primary impressions and fabricating study models in fixed prosthodontics.\n\nEngineered with a Normal Set working time, it provides the perfect, stress-free window to mix, load the tray, and seat it comfortably in the patient's mouth. It is the ideal, cost-effective, and highly reliable choice for dental students and clinicians alike.\nWhy Choose Our Normal Set Alginate?\n\n    Optimized for Primary Impressions: Offers excellent surface detail reproduction, making it perfect for study casts, opposing arch impressions, and fabricating temporary crowns.\n\n    Stress-Free \"Normal Set\" Timing: Gives you ample working time to achieve a smooth, bubble-free mix and perfect tray placement without the rush of fast-setting alternatives.\n\n    High Elasticity & Tear Resistance: Easily withdraws from undercuts without tearing, ensuring the dimensional accuracy of your final plaster model.\n\n    Dust-Free & Easy to Mix: Formulated to mix rapidly into a smooth, homogenous paste, reducing chairside preparation time and cleanup.\n\n    Patient Comfort: Features a pleasant flavor and smooth texture to minimize the gag reflex during impression taking.\n\nProduct Specifications:\n\n    Material Type: Irreversible Hydrocolloid (Alginate).\n\n    Clinical Indication: Primary impressions for crowns & bridges, opposing arch impressions, and diagnostic study models.\n\n    Setting Time: Normal Set (Balanced working and setting phase).\n\n    Pack Size: Standard Moisture-Proof Pouch (Perfect for student courses and daily clinic use).",
