    "price": 150,
    "categoryKey": "clinical",
    "subCategoryKey": "diagostic-kit",
    "description": "Headline: Choosing the Right Dental Mirror: Precision vs. Versatility\nAs a dental professional, your vision is your most valuable asset. The difference between Front Surface and Rear Surface mirrors isn't just a technical detail—it’s about your clinical outcome.\n Front Surface (e.g., Mega, Relax): Engineered for maximum sharpness and clarity. Because the reflection happens on the front layer of the glass, you get a crisp, distortion-free image. This is a must-have for high-precision procedures like crown preparations and operative dentistry.\n Rear Surface (e.g., Standard/Pakistani types): These are excellent for routine examinations. While they may produce a slight double image, they are highly reliable for daily diagnostic tasks.\nGhazal Store Pro Tip: Don't limit your practice to just one. We recommend keeping both in your operatory. Use your Front Surface mirror for delicate restorative work and your Rear Surface mirror for routine check-ups.\nUpgrade your vision today. Explore our dental mirror collection at Ghazal Store.",
