    "arabicName": "Wax Removal",
    "price": 150,
    "categoryKey": "year-3-th",
    "subCategoryKey": "remove",
    "description": "Here is the professional, informative English copywriting for Wax Removal (Wax Elimination / Boil-Out) materials or equipment on your dental e-commerce website.\nWax Removal & Elimination Solutions\nThe Key to Clean, Residue-Free Dental Moulds\nAchieve Perfection in Acrylic Processing\n\nThe success of your final Removable Denture relies entirely on how clean your mold is before packing the acrylic. Any remaining wax residue can compromise the bonding, strength, and shade of the dental appliance.\n\nOur premium Wax Removal solutions and agents are specifically formulated to efficiently melt, dissolve, and wash away all traces of modeling wax and baseplate wax from your gypsum molds during the boil-out stage. It ensures a pristine, clinical-grade surface for flawless acrylic resin adaptation.\nWhy Invest in Our Wax Removal Solutions?\n\n    100% Residue-Free Molds: Completely eliminates wax grease, oils, and synthetic residues from gypsum surfaces, guaranteeing maximum chemical bonding with your heat-cure acrylic.\n\n    Protects Plaster & Stone Integrity: Formulated to clean deeply without softening, eroding, or altering the fine anatomical details of your plaster models or stone casts.\n\n    Enhanced Acrylic Bonding: Prevents tooth pop-outs by ensuring the basal surfaces of your acrylic teeth (like size 16) bond perfectly with the pink acrylic base.\n\n    Time and Effort Saving: Speeds up the boil-out process, making it incredibly easy to rinse away stubborn wax with hot water.\n\n    Safe & Non-Toxic: Eco-friendly and safe for laboratory use, releasing no harsh fumes during the boiling or rinsing phases.\n\nProduct Specifications & Indications:\n\n    Application: Wax elimination (boil-out) for complete dentures, partial dentures, and orthodontic appliances.\n\n    Usage: Ideal for dental laboratory boiling units and manual hot water rinsing.\n\n    Target Audience: Perfect for commercial dental laboratories and dental students in practical prosthetic courses.",
